[VectorDB] save done, cur db size: 110, saved txt: (Convergent evolution is the process where unrelated organisms develop similar traits or characteristics in response to similar environmental pressures. A classic example of convergent evolution is the similarity between the wings of insects and birds, which have evolved independently to serve the same function of flight.)
