[VectorDB] save done, cur db size: 125, saved txt: (The origin of eukaryotic cells occurred when a smaller prokaryotic cell merged with a larger one, leading to the development of internal organelles. This led to an explosion of new life on Earth. Having internal organelles and membranes allows for the separation of specific reactions in the cell, increasing metabolic efficiency.)
